  "htmlContent": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"><title>A boundary can be an act of discernment</title><style>@media only screen and (max-width:620px){.letter{padding-left:24px!important;padding-right:24px!important}.title{font-size:32px!important}.outer{padding:16px 8px!important}}</style></head>\n<body style=\"margin:0;background:#e8dedf;color:#302731\"><div style=\"display:none;max-height:0;overflow:hidden;opacity:0;mso-hide:all\">You can name what you need without claiming to know another person’s motives.</div>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"background:#e8dedf\"><tr><td class=\"outer\" align=\"center\" style=\"padding:40px 16px\">\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"600\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:600px;background:#fcf9f4;border-collapse:collapse\">\n<tr><td style=\"height:6px;background:#653c56;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"letter\" style=\"padding:40px 48px 24px\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 12px;font:11px Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:2px;color:#744b65\">WRITING · TAROT · SPIRITUAL REFLECTION</p><p style=\"margin:0;font:32px/1.2 Georgia,serif;color:#302731\">Letters from Kali</p><div style=\"height:1px;background:#d9ccd2;margin:24px 0 28px\"></div><p style=\"margin:0 0 14px;font:11px Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:2px;color:#744b65\">ON DISCERNMENT · LETTER 05</p><h1 class=\"title\" style=\"margin:0;font:normal 38px/1.15 Georgia,serif;color:#653c56\">A boundary can be an act of discernment.</h1></td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"letter\" style=\"padding:0 48px 40px\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#494048\">Sometimes the question ‘Is this intuition or fear?’ keeps us searching for a certainty we don’t yet have.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#494048\">Meanwhile, a simpler question may be available: What am I willing and able to offer?</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#494048\">Perhaps you need more time before making a commitment. Perhaps you have reached the limit of your energy. Perhaps a request asks for more than you want to give.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#494048\">You don’t need certainty about another person’s motives to name your own limits. A boundary can describe your availability without becoming a verdict about someone else.</p><table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"margin:26px 0;background:#efe5d6;border-left:3px solid #744b65\"><tr><td style=\"padding:24px\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 16px;font:11px Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:2px;color:#744b65\">A MOMENT ON THE PAGE</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#494048\">Choose a small request or commitment you’re considering:</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#494048\">What is being asked of me?</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#494048\">What do I have the time and energy to offer?</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#494048\">What would I need to agree freely?</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#494048\">What could I say clearly and kindly?</p></td></tr></table><p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#494048\">Your answer might sound ordinary: ‘I need a day to think about it.’ ‘I can help with this part.’ ‘I’m not available this week.’</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#494048\">Notice whether you begin inventing a larger explanation to justify a simple need. Put that explanation on the page, too, and ask what you actually know.</p><p style=\"margin:28px 0;font:italic 26px/1.4 Georgia,serif;color:#653c56\">You can be clear about your limits while remaining uncertain about the story.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;color:#494048\">What is one sentence you could use to name a limit this week? You’re welcome to write back.</p><p style=\"margin:30px 0 0;font:italic 30px Georgia,serif;color:#653c56\">Kali</p></td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"letter\" style=\"padding:26px 48px;background:#f5f0e8;border-top:1px solid #d9ccd2;text-align:center;font:12px/1.8 Arial,sans-serif;color:#655b61\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px\">Randi Agency</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px\">11265 Hallett Street, Soddy Daisy, TN 37379</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px\">You&#x27;ve received it because you&#x27;ve subscribed to our newsletter.</p><p style=\"margin:12px 0 0\"><a href=\"{{ unsubscribe }}\" style=\"color:#653c56;text-decoration:underline\">Unsubscribe</a></p></td></tr>\n</table></td></tr></table></body></html>",
